  "notes": "South has a possible loser in both hearts and diamonds. West's spade lead has knocks out dummy's only entry. South must decide whether to finesse in hearts or diamonds.\n\nIf South takes the heart finesse, he may not be out of the woods, even if East has the ♥Q. East may have started with 4 or 5 hearts, in which case he will still get a heart trick. South will have to hope that East or West has a singleton ♦K. If the heart finesse loses, South will again need a miracle in diamonds.\n\nSouth should take the diamond finesse at trick 2. If that finesse works, South can give up a trick to the ♥Q, if necessary, and take the rest of the tricks.\n\nIf the diamond finesse loses, South may still make his contract when the ♥Q drops doubleton or singleton.",
